    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "BROE auctioneers are pleased to present 248 Kilworth Road, a delightful two-bedroom property perfect for first-time buyers or those looking to downsize. Upon entering, you are greeted by a bright hallway that leads to a kitchen overlooking a private garden, providing great outdoor space that is not overlooked. Giving a potential purchaser the option to extend. To the front is a cozy lounge area, ideal for relaxing and entertaining. Upstairs, you’ll find two spacious bedrooms, along with a well-appointed family bathroom featuring contemporary fixtures. \r\nThe location on Kilworth Road is exceptional, offering easy access to amenities such as Our Lady's Children’s Hospital, diverse shopping options, and recreational and educational facilities. The nearby Blackhorse LUAS stop ensures quick access to the City Centre and the M50 motorway. 248 Kilworth Road combines comfortable living with a vibrant community, making it an excellent opportunity for prospective homeowners.\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended. \r\n\r\nFor more information or to register your interest, please contact Shauna O’Brien at BROE auctioneers today."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall\t\t2.85m x 1.76m\t\tNew carpet and understairs storage. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLounge\t\t\t 2.72m x 3.04m\t\tNew carpet and original feature fireplace.               \r\n                       \r\n\r\nKitchen\t\t\t 3.39m x 4.87m\t\tRange of floor & eye level units to include all appliances. Lino flooring. Looking onto private garden.  \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom (1)\t\t\t 3.34m x 4.86m\t\tNew carpet flooring and built in wardrobes and original feature fireplace. \r\n                                                  \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom (2)\t\t\t 3.27m x 2.83m\t\tNew carpet flooring. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBathroom\t\t\t1.96m x 1.51m\t\tPartly tiled bathroom to include bath, WHB & W.C.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nGarden\t\t\t18.00m x 4.80m \t\tSpacious private west facing garden featuring a block shed, backing onto Lansdowne Valley Park. This space is ideal for extending the property while still allowing for a good-sized garden.\r\n\r\n\r\nPlease note we have not tested any appliances, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only.\r\n\r\n\r\nPlease note any information, statement, description, quantity or measurement so given or contained in any such sales particulars, webpage, brochure, catalogue, email, letter, written valuations or hand out issued by or on behalf of BROE auctioneers are for illustration purposes only and are not to be taken as matters of fact. Any mistake, omission, inaccuracy or mis description given orally or contained in any sales particulars, webpage, brochure, catalogue, email, letter, written valuation or hand out issues by BROE auctioneers. Agents shall not give rise to any right of action, claim, entitlement or compensation against BROE auctioneers. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by carrying out their own independent due diligence, inspections or otherwise as to the correctness of any and all the information, statements, descriptions, quantity or measurements contained in any such sales particulars, webpage, brochure, catalogue, email, letter, written valuation or hand out issued by BROE auctioneers. The services, systems and appliances shown have not been tested and no warranty is made or given by BROE auctioneers as to their operability or efficiency."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tDouble Glazed windows. \r\n•\tExcellent location.\r\n•\tWalking distance to the LUAS and numerous bus routes.\r\n•\tConvenient to the City Centre and M50. \r\n•\tBeside a variety of schools and parks. \r\n•\tLarge private west facing rear garden.  \r\n•\tNo onward chain"
